# memfold licensing

memfold is source-available and licensed by component. Each package also declares
its license in its `package.json` and ships its own `LICENSE` file.

## Apache-2.0 (permissive) — implement and build on these freely

- `spec/` — the memfold protocol and the memory-record schema
- `conformance/` — the conformance test suite and vectors
- `packages/core` (`@memfold/core`) — record model, store, retrieval
- `packages/adapters` (`@memfold/adapters`) — per-tool file read/write and compiler
- `packages/mcp` (`@memfold/mcp`) — the MCP server
- `packages/sdk` (`@memfold/sdk`) — the TypeScript SDK and framework adapters

Full text: `LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt`. SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

## FSL-1.1-ALv2 (Functional Source License, Apache-2.0 future) — the server tier

- `packages/daemon` (`@memfold/daemon`) — the local/hostable REST daemon and sync
- `packages/cli` (`memfold`) — the command-line tool

This permits any use except a Competing Use (standing up a product or service that
substitutes for memfold), and it converts to Apache-2.0 two years after each release.
Full text: `LICENSES/FSL-1.1-ALv2.txt`. SPDX-License-Identifier: FSL-1.1-ALv2

## Note

FSL is not an OSI-approved "open source" license, so memfold is described as
"source-available" (or "Fair Source"), not "open source". The specification and the
client SDKs are Apache-2.0 so anyone can implement the protocol and interoperate.
